@startuml arquitectura-despliegue-pysighor
title Arquitectura de Despliegue - pySigHor Web\nStack: React + Spring Boot + PostgreSQL

skinparam linetype polyline

' Definición de nodos de despliegue
node "Cliente (Navegador Web)" as ClientNode {
  artifact "React App\n(Build estático)" as ReactBuild
  component "JavaScript Engine" as JSEngine
  component "HTTP Client" as HttpClient
  
  ReactBuild --> JSEngine
  JSEngine --> HttpClient
}

node "Servidor Web" as WebServer {
  artifact "Nginx" as Nginx {
    note right : Sirve assets estáticos React\nProxy reverso para API\nBalanceador de carga
  }
}

node "Servidor de Aplicación" as AppServer {
  artifact "Spring Boot JAR" as SpringJar {
    component "Embedded Tomcat" as Tomcat
    component "Spring MVC" as SpringMVC
    component "Spring Security" as SpringSecurity
    component "Spring Data JPA" as SpringDataJPA
    
    SpringJar --> Tomcat
    Tomcat --> SpringMVC
    SpringMVC --> SpringSecurity
    SpringMVC --> SpringDataJPA
  }
  
  note right of SpringJar : Implementa 32 casos de uso RUP\nAlgoritmo de optimización 4 fases\nPatrones MVC del análisis
}

node "Servidor de Base de Datos" as DBServer {
  database "PostgreSQL 15" as PostgresDB {
    component "Connection Pool" as ConnPool
    storage "Tablas del Dominio" as DomainTables {
      artifact "programas" as ProgramasTable
      artifact "cursos" as CursosTable  
      artifact "profesores" as ProfesoresTable
      artifact "aulas" as AulasTable
      artifact "edificios" as EdificiosTable
      artifact "recursos" as RecursosTable
      artifact "horarios" as HorariosTable
    }
    
    ConnPool --> DomainTables
  }
  
  note right of PostgresDB : Modelo físico derivado\ndel modelo del dominio RUP\nOptimizado para algoritmo\nde generación de horarios
}

' Servicios de infraestructura
cloud "Servicios Cloud" as CloudServices {
  component "CI/CD Pipeline" as CICD
  component "Monitoring" as Monitoring
  component "Backup Service" as Backup
  component "Email Service" as EmailService
}

' Conexiones de despliegue
ClientNode --> WebServer : "HTTPS\nPuerto 443"
WebServer --> AppServer : "HTTP\nPuerto 8080\n(Proxy reverso)"
AppServer --> DBServer : "JDBC\nPuerto 5432\n(Connection Pool)"

' Servicios externos
AppServer ..> CloudServices : "APIs externas"
DBServer ..> Backup : "Backup automático"
AppServer ..> Monitoring : "Métricas y logs"

' Flujo de datos principal derivado del análisis RUP
note as DataFlow
**Flujo de Datos Típico (Caso de Uso RUP)**
1. Usuario interactúa con React App
2. HTTP Request → Nginx → Spring Boot
3. Spring MVC → Service → Repository
4. JDBC → PostgreSQL → Respuesta
5. JSON → React → UI Update

**Ejemplo: editarCurso()**
- React Form → PUT /api/cursos/{id}
- CursoController → CursoService → CursoRepository  
- UPDATE cursos SET ... WHERE id = ?
- Respuesta JSON → React State Update
end note

' Especificaciones de infraestructura
note as InfraSpecs
**Especificaciones de Infraestructura**

**Servidor Web (Nginx)**
- RAM: 1GB
- CPU: 1 vCore
- Storage: 10GB SSD

**Servidor de Aplicación**
- RAM: 4GB (JVM heap 2-3GB)
- CPU: 2-4 vCores
- Storage: 20GB SSD
- JVM: Java 17 OpenJDK

**Servidor de Base de Datos**
- RAM: 8GB (shared_buffers 2GB)
- CPU: 2-4 vCores  
- Storage: 100GB SSD
- PostgreSQL 15 con extensiones

**Red**
- Latencia < 1ms entre servicios
- Ancho de banda: 1Gbps
- SSL/TLS para comunicación externa
end note

' Configuración de alta disponibilidad (opcional)
package "Configuración HA (Opcional)" as HAConfig {
  node "App Server 2" as AppServer2 {
    artifact "Spring Boot JAR (Replica)" as SpringJar2
  }
  
  node "DB Slave" as DBSlave {
    database "PostgreSQL Replica" as PostgresReplica
  }
  
  WebServer --> AppServer2 : "Load balancing"
  PostgresDB --> PostgresReplica : "Streaming replication"
}

' Variables de entorno y configuración
note as Configuration
**Configuración de Despliegue**

**Spring Boot (application.yml)**
```yaml
server:
  port: 8080
spring:
  datasource:
    url: jdbc:postgresql://db:5432/pysighor
    username: ${DB_USER}
    password: ${DB_PASSWORD}
  jpa:
    hibernate:
      ddl-auto: validate
    show-sql: false
  security:
    jwt:
      secret: ${JWT_SECRET}
```

**Nginx (nginx.conf)**
```nginx
upstream backend {
  server app:8080;
}

server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://backend;
  }
  location / {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
  }
}
```
end note

' Docker Compose para desarrollo local
note as DockerCompose
**Docker Compose (Desarrollo Local)**

```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  db:
    image: postgres:15
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: pysighor
      POSTGRES_USER: ${DB_USER}
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD}
    ports:
      - "5432:5432"
    volumes:
      - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data

  backend:
    build: ./backend
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"
    depends_on:
      - db
    environment:
      DB_HOST: db
      DB_USER: ${DB_USER}
      DB_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD}

  frontend:
    build: ./frontend  
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    depends_on:
      - backend
```
end note

@enduml